+# Performance history
+
+## UserPromptSubmit read path
+
+The repository does not contain a measured full-recall `UserPromptSubmit` p95
+for the adversarial synthetic corpus before the term-selection fix. Accordingly,
+no pre-fix number is reported here.
+
+The fix was to change prompt-term selection so that a term is omitted when it
+occurs in more than one third of the active records (for stores with at least 50
+records). Such terms carry little discriminating information in the synthetic
+30-word vocabulary and force FTS5 to traverse long posting lists. The remaining
+terms are ranked by IDF and the best eight are passed to BM25.
+
+The repository also does not contain a measured post-fix full-recall
+`UserPromptSubmit` p95 for that adversarial synthetic corpus, so no post-fix
+number is reported here. The other p95 values documented in the research notes
+use different corpora or read paths and are not substitutes for this
+before/after measurement.
